# The getting-started page was published at /docs/get-started/ first. The name
# changed, the page did not.
/docs/get-started*      /docs/getting-started/                                                    301

# Pages that used to be hosted and now live in the repository. A redirect is
# kinder than a 404: these URLs were public, and the documents still exist.
#
# The splat sits directly against the name rather than after a slash. Pages only
# rewrites /docs/x to /docs/x/ when that directory is still deployed, so for a
# page that has been removed the slashless form reaches no rule at all.
/docs/opencode*         /docs/harnesses/                                                          301
/docs/conformance*      https://github.com/larstonder/whippletree/blob/main/docs/CONFORMANCE.md    301
/docs/maintenance*      https://github.com/larstonder/whippletree/blob/main/MAINTENANCE.md         301
/docs/probes*           https://github.com/larstonder/whippletree/tree/main/docs                   301

# No catch-all. A /* -> /index.html 200 rule makes every wrong URL look like the
# homepage, so nobody ever learns they are lost.
#
# The Go vanity import still resolves without one: the go tool probes the full
# package path first and walks up to shorter prefixes when that fails, and the
# root serves the go-import meta tag. 404.html carries it too, so even the
# failing probe answers correctly.
